    <p>ZINNIASHARK ("ZINNIASHARK," "we," "us," or "our") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle information when you visit <strong>zinniashark.com</strong> or contact us by email.</p>
    <h2>1. Who We Are</h2><p><strong>Legal business name:</strong> 지니아샥(ZINNIASHARK)<br /><strong>Representative:</strong> DAESHIK YI<br /><strong>Address:</strong> 404, Jueun Art Villa, 1, Jinmok 2-gil, Geoje-si, Gyeongsangnam-do 53224, Republic of Korea<br /><strong>Privacy contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@zinniashark.com">contact@zinniashark.com</a></p>
    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2><p>When you contact us, we may receive your name, email address, message contents, and files or information you voluntarily provide. Hosting and security providers may process limited technical information such as IP address, browser type, device information, and request logs to deliver, secure, and maintain the Website.</p><p>Do not send passwords, financial information, or other sensitive information by email.</p>
    <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2><ul><li>Respond to inquiries and provide support;</li><li>Communicate about ZINNIASHARK products when you ask us to;</li><li>Operate, maintain, and protect the Website;</li><li>Detect, prevent, and investigate abuse or security incidents; and</li><li>Comply with applicable laws.</li></ul>
    <h2>4. Cookies and Analytics</h2><p>As of the effective date, the Website does not intentionally use advertising cookies or third-party analytics for behavioral profiling. Essential technical processing by hosting or security providers may still occur when the Website is delivered. If we introduce analytics, marketing cookies, contact forms, or newsletters, we will update this Policy.</p>
    <h2>5. Sharing and Service Providers</h2><p>We do not sell personal information. We may share limited information with providers that host, secure, operate, or support the Website, as reasonably necessary. We may disclose information when required by law or necessary to protect our rights, users, or the public.</p>
    <h2>6. Retention and Your Requests</h2><p>We retain inquiry-related information only as long as reasonably necessary to respond, provide support, resolve disputes, maintain business records, or comply with legal obligations. You may contact us to ask about, correct, or request deletion of personal information where applicable. We may verify your identity before completing a request.</p>
    <h2>7. Security, Children, and International Processing</h2><p>We use reasonable administrative and technical measures to protect information, but no method is completely secure. The Website is not directed to children under the age at which they can provide valid consent under applicable law. Hosting or security providers may process information outside the Republic of Korea with appropriate safeguards where applicable.</p>
    <h2>8. Changes and Contact</h2><p>We may update this Policy and will post the revised version with a new effective date. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:contact@zinniashark.com">contact@zinniashark.com</a>.</p>
